s nuclear program there were  a lot of question marks about Iran's  program now we have exclamation points  that they had a military nuclear program  and they had an intention and they still  have an intention to ultimately build a  nuclear weapon but mr. ambassador it was  Israeli policy and US policy that Iran  has been consistently lying about this  weapons program and so while there is  new details and fascinating new tales  about the nature and corners and  crannies of that lie the basic fact that  that everybody knew and was operating on  the fact they were lying is is still  something everybody knew well some  people knew that they were lying not  everybody there were inspectors there  were nuclear experts who claimed as of a  few years ago that Iran really didn't  have a military nuclear program so  hopefully this will be news to them but  I'll tell you John I think what was said  before that this is not a violation of  the deal is simply wrong what this  proves conclusively is that Iran  falsified all of their reports to the  International Atomic Energy Agency which  was critical for them to move forward  with the deal in addition to that they  have taken efforts since the deal to  hide this nuclear weapons program you  know I referred to this deal what  Netanyahu  yesterday about this nuclear deal as a  smoking bomb why did I say it not just  the smoking gun because you know in the  play you see the smoking gun in the  first act and then it goes off in the  later act what you see now is Iran has  all of these files in a vault they  didn't destroy them which they could  have they could have come clean about  their program in the past what they have  is all these files in the vault so when  these nuclear restrictions are removed  they can then go to those vaults and use  it to build a nuclear arsenal that's why  this deal is so dangerous ambassador the  Iranian program to design and build  nuclear weapons was hardly a secret  that's why the President Obama went  forward with this Iranian deal the key  question that many people have this  morning do the Israelis have any  evidence that Iran is currently not in  compliance with the deal I just told you  the evidence they are actively engaged  in an effort to hide their military  nuclear program and what you said also I  would dispute as well the question is  why would Iran keep this these files  because they're going to use it in the  future now a lot of people responded to  what Netanyahu said yesterday said hey  we knew all this we knew that Iran was  lying and that's why we need these  restrictions in place that would be a  reasonable argument Nora  if these restrictions did not end but  they end in a few years they are  automatically gonna be removed in a few  years what I would hope let me just  finish this one sense what I would hope  that everybody who supported the deal  before would do today is say we need  those restrictions to never end because  Iran clearly has a desire not just to  build nuclear weapons in the past which  we knew but to build nuclear weapons in  the future because they're keeping it in  a safe for safekeeping  in the future when those restrictions  are removed but that's their stated  policy which is that if the u.s. pulls  out of the deal or the deal changes  they'll restart their nuclear program  now whether they'd call it a peaceful  program or not but that's their stated  stated policy so is that a surprise to  anybody that they would restart this  program if the deal fell apart well they  may decide to restart their program but  we're not concerned that they're going  to break out to a bomb the big danger of  the deal John and this is not something  Israel saying today it's something the  prime minister said three years ago in  Congress the greater danger is not that  he  is going to get to a single nuclear bomb  by violating the deal the biggest danger  of this deal is that they can get to an  entire nuclear arsenal by keeping the  deal when all of these restrictions are  removed and no one is talking about the  price you paid for this deal which is  the removal on the the removal of the  sanctions on on Iran sanctions that were  preventing Iran from running throughout  the Middle East and conquering countries  this is what they're doing in Iraq in  Syria in Lebanon in Yemen so this  sanction relief has actually fueled  Iran's war machine and that's why this  deal is so dangerous and that's why it's  so important for the international  community to unite now behind clear  demands that Iran fully dismantle its  nuclear program and if they don't they  should ratchet up these sanctions you  ambassador do you have 100% certainty  from this White House that President  Trump is gonna withdraw from the deal  well it's ultimately gonna be president  Trump's decision and he hasn't said what  he's going to do I think it's clear what  the direction of the policy is I think  the change today from yesterday is I  think it's likely that more of your  allies will follow ultimately his  decision because the revelations that  the Prime Minister presented yesterday  will give a bridge to those who  supported this deal to walk over to the  US side and to make clear demands on  Iran moving forward  all right ambassador Dermer thank you so  much for being with us
 

